+/*
+ * Round262. The wait rows this sampler already prints are filtered: they name
+ * up to six threads that are waiting and not in the trap, and they say nothing
+ * about how many threads the task has or what the rest are doing. The census is
+ * the unfiltered pass -- every thread, its state, the event it blocks on and the
+ * continuation that would wake it -- so the question r261 left open can be
+ * answered by a reading instead of a guess: the dispatch group that never drains
+ * is owed one leave, and whoever owes it is either asleep on that very word (then
+ * the census shows a second sleeper on the same address) or idle and never handed
+ * the block (then it shows a thread with no wait event at all). Sheng answers the
+ * same question with package/BootUiTraceProbe.c, which walks cross-task with the
+ * native VM API and names the hot threads by context-switch rate and run time;
+ * that shape is what this pass copies, minus the weights, because one beat has to
+ * fit the card's last 512 kernel rows.
+ */
+#define CLOVER_BB_CENSUS 14
+
